\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Effective half-life as a function of the two adaptive triggers, evaluated by calling \texttt  {\small  effective\_half\_life} over a grid. Inside both thresholds (lower-left block) the factor is exactly $1$ and the baseline 6-hour half-life is preserved bit-for-bit. Either trigger alone shortens it; the surface saturates at the configured floor $t_{\min } = 30$ minutes. The two mechanisms are combined by $\max $, not by summation, so a market that is both busy and moving is not double-counted.}}{6}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:halflife}{{3}{6}{Effective half-life as a function of the two adaptive triggers, evaluated by calling \code {effective\_half\_life} over a grid. Inside both thresholds (lower-left block) the factor is exactly $1$ and the baseline 6-hour half-life is preserved bit-for-bit. Either trigger alone shortens it; the surface saturates at the configured floor $t_{\min } = 30$ minutes. The two mechanisms are combined by $\max $, not by summation, so a market that is both busy and moving is not double-counted}{figure.caption.6}{}}
